{"4965510": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Escape Sequence", "steam_appid": 4965510, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<strong>The freeway runs along the ocean, the sun refuses to set, and somewhere in<br>your mirror there's a driver who plays the game the way you do.</strong><br><br>Escape Sequence is an endless synthwave driver in the spirit of the arcade<br>classics — curves that lean, hills that breathe, traffic that flows like sheet<br>music — rebuilt around one idea: <strong>the road is a score, and everyone plays<br>the same one.</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >WILD DRIVERS — RIVALS WHO ARE ALIVE</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>AI drivers hunt you from behind, weave the same traffic, fight the same<br>storms and the same centrifugal pull — and sometimes lose, spectacularly.<br></li><li>Brush past a rival for bonus flow; outlast them and take their legend.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >THE NEAR-MISS IS THE MELODY</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Graze traffic to build near-miss chains: ×2, ×3… ×8 — flow is score and<br>score is currency.<br></li><li>Slipstream behind civilians for a burst of speed. Ride the oncoming lanes<br>if you dare — the pay is better on the wrong side of the road.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A ROAD WRITTEN BY A SEED</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Every run's highway grows from one number: same seed, same traffic, same<br>weather fronts, same curves — frame by frame, on every machine.<br></li><li>Day turns to night, rain turns to storm, and the coast forks into desert<br>and neon city. Your lane at the gantry chooses the world ahead.<br></li><li>Three highway profiles: a lonely 1+1 coastal road, a 2+2 expressway, the<br>full 3+3 boulevard — pick one or let the seed roll.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >MULTIPLAYER WITHOUT EXCUSES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Steam invites</strong> — host, open the overlay, race a friend through<br>Valve's relay. No IPs, no port forwarding.<br></li><li><strong>Public games</strong> — host a public lobby or browse the list and jump in.<br></li><li><strong>Score Duel, Last Sequence, Knockout</strong> — everyone drives the same<br>seed; ghosts can't hurt you (optional bump mode if the lobby votes danger).<br></li><li>Honest LAN for the same couch, same switch, same night.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SOLO DISCIPLINES</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Endless</strong> — the wall comes for everyone; the leaderboard remembers.<br></li><li><strong>Checkpoint Run</strong> — the clock is the enemy. <strong>Time Attack</strong> — two<br>minutes, every near-miss buys another second. <strong>Cruise</strong> — no stakes,<br>just the ocean.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >EVERYTHING FROM CODE</h2>Every car, palm and thunderhead is built from code; every sound is synthesized<br>in-engine over an original synthwave soundtrack. A garage of six machines with<br>one law: identical hitbox — buying speed never buys safety. CRT filters<br>included, for those who remember.<br><br><i>Keyboard or gamepad. Solo, LAN, and online for up to 4 pilots.</i><br>", "about_the_game": "<strong>The freeway runs along the ocean, the sun refuses to set, and somewhere in<br>your mirror there's a driver who plays the game the way you do.</strong><br><br>Escape Sequence is an endless synthwave driver in the spirit of the arcade<br>classics — curves that lean, hills that breathe, traffic that flows like sheet<br>music — rebuilt around one idea: <strong>the road is a score, and everyone plays<br>the same one.</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >WILD DRIVERS — RIVALS WHO ARE ALIVE</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>AI drivers hunt you from behind, weave the same traffic, fight the same<br>storms and the same centrifugal pull — and sometimes lose, spectacularly.<br></li><li>Brush past a rival for bonus flow; outlast them and take their legend.</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >THE NEAR-MISS IS THE MELODY</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Graze traffic to build near-miss chains: ×2, ×3… 